# SANGAM — frontend environment
#
# You almost certainly do NOT need to set anything here.
#
# By default the app calls the API at a RELATIVE path (/api/…), which the Vite
# dev server proxies to the engine on 127.0.0.1:8001. That works on localhost
# and through a forwarded port without any configuration, because the browser
# only ever talks to one origin.
#
# Copy to .env.local ONLY if the engine is genuinely on a different origin —
# a deployed backend, for example.
#
#   VITE_API_BASE=https://engine.example.gov.in
#
# Do NOT point this at a dev-tunnel URL. Doing so makes the browser issue a
# cross-origin, cross-site request: the session cookie then needs
# SameSite=None, the CORS allowlist has to track a tunnel ID that expires, and
# localhost breaks because one static value cannot serve two origins. The proxy
# exists precisely so none of that is necessary.

# Where the Vite dev server proxies /api to. Change only if the engine is not
# on this machine or not on port 8001.
# VITE_ENGINE_ORIGIN=http://127.0.0.1:8001

# Never put a secret in a VITE_* variable — they are inlined into the bundle
# and are readable by anyone who opens the site.
